 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A Category 4 hurricane is sliding past Mexico's resorts. Will it make landfall?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Hurricane Simon grew to Category 4 off Mexico's Pacific coast, news outlets report. Mexico's weather service said it was moving parallel to the shore, less than fifty kilometers from Jalisco, rather than making direct landfall for now."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Jalisco put Puerto Vallarta and twenty-one other municipalities under its highest alert. Authorities closed ports, including Manzanillo, and Puerto Vallarta's airport. Mexico's Security Ministry counted five hundred seventy-nine people evacuated or sheltered across three states, an early figure."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "So why the doubt? CNN reports the storm's path shifted and is hard to predict. The National Hurricane Center said it is unclear whether Simon will come ashore, which could let it keep its strength. Forecasters warn of life-threatening flooding and mudslides."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Simon make landfall on Mexico's coast this week? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
